# Bellwether: code is versioned, data is not.
#
# Everything ignored here is either regenerable from the immutable snapshots or
# far too large for git (the database alone is 2.2GB and one archive member is
# 410MB, well past GitHub's 100MB per-file limit). Committing any of it once
# would bloat the repo permanently, since git keeps every version forever.
#
# It also matters for privacy: the database and the web cache hold names, email
# addresses and phone numbers of real people at thousands of firms. That is our
# working data, not source code, and it does not belong in a shared repo.

# --- the database and everything derived from it -------------------------
prospect.db
prospect.db-wal
prospect.db-shm
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm

# --- captured source data, caches, runtime state -------------------------
data/

# --- secrets -------------------------------------------------------------
# Real values live in the environment or in a .env that never leaves the box.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
config/users.yml
secret_key

# --- generated assets ----------------------------------------------------
assets/*.ico

# --- python --------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
env/

# --- editors and OS ------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# --- logs ----------------------------------------------------------------
*.log

# --- superseded prototypes, kept on disk but never committed ---------------
# The four original scripts this project grew out of. Excluded for three
# reasons: they are fully replaced by prospect/ and scripts/, they depend on
# pandas, bs4 and local CSVs that are not part of this system, and
# "Mailwarm API.py" carries a live API key in a URL. A secret committed once
# stays in git history forever, so it never gets committed at all.
13F Form scraper.py
ADV Form scraper.py
Mailwarm API.py
product_fit_scoring.py
